[Term]
id: ARO:0000015
name: methicillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Derived from penicillin to combat penicillin-resistance, methicillin is insensitive to beta-lactamases (also known as penicillinases) secreted by many penicillin-resistant bacteria. Methicillin is bactericidal, and acts by inhibiting the synthesis of the peptidoglycan layer of bacterial cell walls. The peptidoglycan layer is important for cell wall structural integrity, especially in Gram-positive organisms." [PMID:15673804, PMID:3889939, PMID:11585791]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "Dimocillin" EXACT []
synonym: "Metacillin" EXACT []
