name: antibiotic molecule
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Antibiotics are commonly classified based on their mechanism of action, chemical structure or spectrum of activity." []
is_a: ARO:1000001 ! process or component of antibiotic biology or chemistry

[Term]
id: ARO:3000000
name: determinant of antibiotic resistance
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "A mutation, single nucleotide polymorphism, gene, or gene product that confers antibiotic resistance." [PMID:15700955]
is_a: ARO:1000001 ! process or component of antibiotic biology or chemistry

[Term]
id: ARO:3000003
name: antibiotic without defined classification
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "These compounds are antibiotics of unique structure or origin, without a defined classification." []
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
synonym: "miscellaneous antibiotic" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000007
name: beta-lactam antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Beta-lactam antibiotics are a broad class of antibiotics that include penams (penicillin derivatives), cephems (cephalosporins), monobactams, and carbapenems. These antibiotic agents contain a beta-lactam nucleus in its molecular structure. They are the most widely-used group of antibiotics." [PMID:3889939]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule

[Term]
id: ARO:3000008
name: penam
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Penams, often referred to as penicillins, are a group of antibiotics derived from Penicillium fungi. Penicillin antibiotics are historically significant because they are the first drugs that were effective against many previously serious diseases such as syphilis and Staphylococcus infections. Penicillins are still widely used today, though many types of bacteria are now resistant. All penicillins are beta-lactam antibiotics in the penam sub-group, and are used in the treatment of bacterial infections caused by susceptible, usually Gram-positive, organisms." [PMID:3889939]
is_a: ARO:3000007 ! beta-lactam antibiotic
synonym: "penicillin" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000012
name: protein(s) conferring antibiotic resistance via molecular bypass
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Proteins involved in restructuring of the cell wall, causing antibiotic resistance." []
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:3000213 ! restructuring of bacterial cell wall conferring antibiotic resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000036
name: tetracycline inactivation enzyme
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Enzymes or other gene products which hydroxylate tetracycline and other tetracycline derivatives. Hydroxylation inactivates tetracycline-like antibiotics, thus conferring resistance to these compounds." [PMID:24497223]
is_a: ARO:3000557 ! antibiotic inactivation enzyme
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000050 ! tetracycline antibiotic
relationship: participates_in ARO:3000450 ! hydroxylation of antibiotic conferring resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000050
name: tetracycline antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "These antibiotics are derived from tetracycline, a polyketide antibiotic that inhibits the 30S subunit of bacterial ribosomes." [PMID:11381101]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule

[Term]
id: ARO:3000081
name: glycopeptide antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Glycopeptide antibiotics are natural products produced non-ribosomally by Actinomycetales bacteria. With the exception of bleomycins, they act by binding the terminal D-Ala-D-Ala in peptidoglycan precursors of the growing bacterial cell wall and are generally active against Gram-positive bacteria.  This inhibits transglycosylation leading to cell death due to osmotic stress." [PMID:3276316, PMID:4369274, PMID:16007453, PMID:10232990]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule

[Term]
id: ARO:3000100
name: gene modulating beta-lactam resistance
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Genes that directly or indirectly modulate beta-lactam resistance." [PMID:16143832]
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000112
name: multidrug and toxic compound extrusion (MATE) transporter
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Directed pumping of antibiotic out of a cell to confer resistance. Multidrug and toxic compound extrusion (MATE) transporters utilize the cationic gradient across the membrane as an energy source. Although there is a diverse substrate specificity, almost all MATE transporters recognize fluoroquinolones. Arciflavine, ethidium and aminoglycosides are also good substrates." [PMID:16330770, PMID:19100867]
is_a: ARO:3000159 ! efflux pump complex or subunit conferring antibiotic resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000124
name: mecI
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "mecI acts as a repressor of transcription of the mecA/mecR1/mecI operon." [PMID:24564530]
is_a: ARO:3000100 ! gene modulating beta-lactam resistance
relationship: part_of ARO:3000268 ! mec operon
relationship: regulates ARO:3000617 ! mecA
relationship: regulates ARO:3001209 ! mecC

[Term]
id: ARO:3000157
name: rifamycin antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Rifamycin antibiotics are a group of broad-spectrum ansamycin antibiotics that inhibit bacterial RNA polymerase by binding to a highly conserved region, blocking the oligonucleotide exit tunnel, and preventing the extension of nascent mRNAs." [PMID:15700959]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule

[Term]
id: ARO:3000159
name: efflux pump complex or subunit conferring antibiotic resistance
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Efflux proteins that pump antibiotic out of a cell to confer resistance." []
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:0010000 ! antibiotic efflux

[Term]
id: ARO:3000169
name: rifampin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Rifampin is a semi-synthetic rifamycin, and inhibits RNA synthesis by binding to RNA polymerase. Rifampin is the mainstay agent for the treatment of tuberculosis, leprosy and complicated Gram-positive infections." [PMID:6356275, PMID:15667909]
is_a: ARO:3000157 ! rifamycin antibiotic
synonym: "rifampicin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:135398735

[Term]
id: ARO:3000170
name: imipenem
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Imipenem is a broad-spectrum antibiotic and is usually taken with cilastatin, which prevents hydrolysis of imipenem by renal dehydropeptidase-I. It is resistant to hydrolysis by most other beta-lactamases. Notable exceptions are the KPC beta-lactamases and Ambler Class B enzymes." [PMID:10629005, PMID:12084099]
is_a: ARO:0000020 ! carbapenem
xref: PubChem:104838

[Term]
id: ARO:3000171
name: diaminopyrimidine antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Diaminopyrimidines are a class of organic compounds containing a pyrimidine ring substituted by two amine groups.  They are inhibitors of dihydrofolate reductase, an enzyme critical for DNA synthesis." [PMID:8195830]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
synonym: "diaminopyrimidine" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000185
name: antibiotic target protection protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "These proteins confer antibiotic resistance by bind the antibiotic target to prevent antibiotic binding." []
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:0001003 ! antibiotic target protection

[Term]
id: ARO:3000188
name: trimethoprim
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Trimethoprim is a synthetic 5-(3,4,5- trimethoxybenzyl) pyrimidine inhibitor of dihydrofolate reductase, inhibiting synthesis of tetrahydrofolic acid. Tetrahydrofolic acid is an essential precursor in the de novo synthesis of the DNA nucleotide thymidine. Trimethoprim is a bacteriostatic antibiotic mainly used in the prophylaxis and treatment of urinary tract infections in combination with sulfamethoxazole, a sulfonamide antibiotic." [PMID:18024520, PMID:11432417]
is_a: ARO:3000171 ! diaminopyrimidine antibiotic
xref: PubChem:5578

[Term]
id: ARO:3000213
name: restructuring of bacterial cell wall conferring antibiotic resistance
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Peptidoglycan precursors ending in D-Ala-D-Lac or D-Ala-D-Ser instead of D-Ala-D-Ala conferring high level glycopeptide resistance." [PMID:9177243, PMID:1931965]
is_a: ARO:0001001 ! antibiotic target alteration
synonym: "molecular bypass conferring antibiotic resistance" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000231
name: beta-lactam resistance operon
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "An operon conferring resistance to beta-lactam antibiotics." []
is_a: ARO:0000010 ! antibiotic resistance gene cluster, cassette, or operon

[Term]
id: ARO:3000234
name: glycopeptide resistance gene cluster
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Genes that when expressed confer resistance to vancomycin and teicoplanin type antibiotics." [PMID:16323116]
is_a: ARO:0000010 ! antibiotic resistance gene cluster, cassette, or operon
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000081 ! glycopeptide antibiotic
relationship: participates_in ARO:3000213 ! restructuring of bacterial cell wall conferring antibiotic resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000238
name: glycopeptide resistance gene cluster VanB
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "This inducible cluster confers resistance to vancomycin but organisms remain sensitive to teicoplanin by allowing restructuring of peptidoglycan precursors to end in D-Ala-D-Lac.  Sensitivity to teicoplanin is due to lack of binding to the sensor kinase VanS. The vanB gene cluster can be located either on plasmids or on the chromosome. Gene orientation: vanRSYWHBX" [PMID:16323116, PMID:8654967]
is_a: ARO:3000234 ! glycopeptide resistance gene cluster

[Term]
id: ARO:3000244
name: reduced permeability to antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Reduction in permeability to antibiotic, generally through reduced production of porins, can provide resistance." [PMID:19100346, PMID:2848006]
is_a: ARO:1000002 ! mechanism of antibiotic resistance

[Term]
id: ARO:3000245
name: RbpA
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "RNA-polymerase binding protein which confers resistance to rifampin." [PMID:16629670, PMID:21415119]
is_a: ARO:3004243 ! RbpA bacterial RNA polymerase-binding protein
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000169 ! rifampin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000517 ! rifaximin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000530 ! rifabutin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000534 ! rifapentine

[Term]
id: ARO:3000257
name: glycopeptide resistance gene cluster VanG
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Contains a D-Ala-D-Ser ligase. The vanG gene cluster is inducible and confers low resistance to vancomycin. vanG organisms remain susceptible to teicoplanin. It is the only van gene cluster that contains two vanY genes. Gene orientation: vanRSYWGYT" [PMID:16323116, PMID:19851013, PMID:11036060]
is_a: ARO:3000234 ! glycopeptide resistance gene cluster

[Term]
id: ARO:3000263
name: marA
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "In the presence of antibiotic stress, E. coli overexpresses the global activator protein MarA, which besides inducing MDR efflux pump AcrAB, also down- regulates synthesis of the porin OmpF." [PMID:9333027, PMID:2848006, PMID:12027588]
is_a: ARO:3000270 ! protein modulating permeability to antibiotic
is_a: ARO:3000451 ! protein(s) and two-component regulatory system modulating antibiotic efflux
relationship: regulates ARO:3000265 ! porin OmpF
relationship: regulates ARO:3000384 ! AcrAB-TolC

[Term]
id: ARO:3000265
name: porin OmpF
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "In the presence of antibiotic stress, E. coli overexpresses the global activator protein MarA, which besides inducing MDR efflux pump AcrAB, also down- regulates synthesis of the porin OmpF." [PMID:2848006, PMID:19100346]
is_a: ARO:3004281 ! General Bacterial Porin with reduced permeability to beta-lactams

[Term]
id: ARO:3000268
name: mec operon
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "The mec operon is composed of mecA/mecR1/mecI." []
is_a: ARO:3000231 ! beta-lactam resistance operon

[Term]
id: ARO:3000269
name: brodimoprim
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Brodimoprim is a structural derivative of trimethoprim and an inhibitor of bacterial dihydrofolate reductase. The 4-methoxy group of trimethoprim is replaced with a bromine atom." [PMID:7562018, PMID:8195838, PMID:10026296]
is_a: ARO:3000171 ! diaminopyrimidine antibiotic
xref: PubChem:68760

[Term]
id: ARO:3000270
name: protein modulating permeability to antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Enzymes or other proteins either directly or indirectly reducing overall permeability to antibiotics." [PMID:2848006, PMID:19100346]
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:3000244 ! reduced permeability to antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3000276
name: cephem
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cephems have a six-membered dihydrothiazine ring with a sulfur atom and double bond fused with its beta-lactam ring. This group includes the cephalosporins and cephamycins, the latter containing an additional alpha-methoxy group." []
is_a: ARO:3000007 ! beta-lactam antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3000284
name: tetroxoprim
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Tetroxoprim is a trimethoprim derivative that inhibits bacterial dihydrofolate reductase." [PMID:7036848, PMID:3043259]
is_a: ARO:3000171 ! diaminopyrimidine antibiotic
xref: PubChem:65450

[Term]
id: ARO:3000337
name: iclaprim
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Iclaprim is a bactericidal compound that inhibits dihydrofolate reductase. It is used against clinically important Gram-positive pathogens, including methicillin-sensitive Staphylococcus aureus and methicillin-resistant S. aureus." [PMID:19622858, PMID:19289528]
is_a: ARO:3000171 ! diaminopyrimidine antibiotic
synonym: "AR-100" EXACT []
synonym: "RO-48-2622" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:213043

[Term]
id: ARO:3000373
name: EmrKY-TolC
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "EmrKY is a homolog of EmrAB found in E. coli. Together with TolC, it is a tripartite multidrug transporter." []
is_a: ARO:0010002 ! major facilitator superfamily (MFS) antibiotic efflux pump
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000051 ! tetracycline

[Term]
id: ARO:3000381
name: antibiotic target replacement protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Alternate proteins that have the same functions as other antibiotic target proteins, but are structurally different and thus resistant to antibiotics. These can replace the activity of other antibiotic-sensitive proteins in the presence of antibiotics." []
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:0001002 ! antibiotic target replacement

[Term]
id: ARO:3000384
name: AcrAB-TolC
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "AcrAB-TolC is a tripartite RND efflux system that confers resistance to tetracycline, chloramphenicol, ampicillin, nalidixic acid, and rifampin  in Gram-negative bacteria. The system spans the cell membrane (AcrB) and the outer-membrane (TolC), and is linked together in the periplasm by AcrA." [PMID:8550435, PMID:21513882]
is_a: ARO:0010004 ! resistance-nodulation-cell division (RND) antibiotic efflux pump
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000030 ! tigecycline
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000051 ! tetracycline
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000169 ! rifampin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000385 ! chloramphenicol
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000637 ! ampicillin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000704 ! cefalotin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000870 ! triclosan
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3000385
name: chloramphenicol
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Chloramphenicol is a bacteriostatic antimicrobial originally derived from the bacterium Streptomyces venezuelae. It was the first antibiotic to be manufactured synthetically on a large scale. It functions by inhibiting peptidyl transferase activity of the bacterial ribosome, binding to A2451 and A2452 residues in the 23S rRNA of the 50S ribosomal subunit and preventing peptide bond formation." [PMID:17737966]
is_a: ARO:3000387 ! phenicol antibiotic
synonym: "CHL" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5959

[Term]
id: ARO:3000387
name: phenicol antibiotic
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Phenicols are broad spectrum bacteriostatic antibiotics acting on bacterial protein synthesis. More specifically, the phenicols block peptide elongation by binding to the peptidyltansferase centre of the 70S ribosome." [PMID:12860128]
is_a: ARO:1000003 ! antibiotic molecule
synonym: "phenicol" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000419
name: quinolone resistance protein (qnr)
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Qnr proteins are pentapeptide repeat proteins that mimic DNA and protect the cell from the activity of fluoroquinolone antibiotics" [PMID:19822894, PMID:15933203, PMID:19258263]
is_a: ARO:3000185 ! antibiotic target protection protein
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000036 ! ciprofloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000071 ! levofloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000074 ! moxifloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000659 ! gatifloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000661 ! nalidixic acid
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000662 ! norfloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:3000666 ! sparfloxacin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
synonym: "Qnr" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000450
name: hydroxylation of antibiotic conferring resistance
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Inactivation of an antibiotic via introduction a hydroxyl group (-OH)." []
is_a: ARO:0001004 ! antibiotic inactivation

[Term]
id: ARO:3000451
name: protein(s) and two-component regulatory system modulating antibiotic efflux
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Protein(s) and two component regulatory systems that directly or indirectly change rates of antibiotic efflux." [PMID:14572535, PMID:24878531]
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:0010000 ! antibiotic efflux

[Term]
id: ARO:3000503
name: AcrEF-TolC
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "AcrEF-TolC is a tripartite multidrug efflux system similar to AcrAB-TolC and found in Gram-negative bacteria. AcrE is the membrane fusion protein, AcrF is the inner membrane transporter, and TolC is the outer membrane channel protein." [PMID:18984645, PMID:1720861, PMID:8647368, PMID:12937021, PMID:16267305]
is_a: ARO:0010004 ! resistance-nodulation-cell division (RND) antibiotic efflux pump
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000044 ! cephamycin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "EnvCD-TolC" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000507
name: rifampin-resistant RNA polymerase-binding protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Proteins which have been experimentally shown to protect RNA-polymerase from rifampin inhibition." []
is_a: ARO:3000185 ! antibiotic target protection protein

[Term]
id: ARO:3000517
name: rifaximin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Rifaximin is a semi-synthetic rifamycin used to treat traveller's diarrhea. Rifaximin inhibits RNA synthesis by binding to the beta subunit of bacterial RNA polymerase." [PMID:15667909]
is_a: ARO:3000157 ! rifamycin antibiotic
xref: PubChem:6436173

[Term]
id: ARO:3000530
name: rifabutin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Rifabutin is a semisynthetic rifamycin used in tuberculosis therapy. It inhibits DNA-dependent RNA synthesis." [PMID:15700959]
is_a: ARO:3000157 ! rifamycin antibiotic
xref: PubChem:135398743

[Term]
id: ARO:3000534
name: rifapentine
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Rifapentine is a semisynthetic rifamycin that inhibits DNA-dependent RNA synthesis. It is often used in the treatment of tuberculosis and leprosy." [PMID:15700959]
is_a: ARO:3000157 ! rifamycin antibiotic
synonym: "priftin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:135403821

[Term]
id: ARO:3000550
name: aztreonam
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Aztreonam was the first monobactam discovered, and is greatly effective against Gram-negative bacteria while inactive against Gram-positive bacteria. Artreonam is a poor substrate for beta-lactamases, and may even act as an inhibitor. In Gram-negative bacteria, Aztreonam interferes with filamentation, inhibiting cell division and leading to cell death." [PMID:3871589]
is_a: ARO:0000004 ! monobactam
synonym: "ATM" EXACT []
synonym: "Primbactam" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5742832

[Term]
id: ARO:3000557
name: antibiotic inactivation enzyme
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Enzyme that catalyzes the inactivation of an antibiotic resulting in resistance.  Inactivation includes chemical modification, destruction, etc." []
is_a: ARO:3000000 ! determinant of antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:0001004 ! antibiotic inactivation

[Term]
id: ARO:3000575
name: vanU
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "VanU is a transcriptional activator of vancomycin resistance genes." [PMID:14617152, PMID:11036060]
is_a: ARO:3002976 ! gene(s) or protein(s) associated with a glycopeptide resistance cluster
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000081 ! glycopeptide antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3000617
name: mecA
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "A foreign PBP2a acquired by lateral gene transfer that able to perform peptidoglycan synthesis in the presence of beta-lactams." [PMID:6563036, PMID:12389036, PMID:21636525, PMID:21931689, PMID:27547406, PMID:18718557, PMID:15226303, PMID:3878127, PMID:2708325]
is_a: ARO:3001208 ! methicillin resistant PBP2
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000015 ! methicillin
synonym: "PBP2A" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3000632
name: benzylpenicillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Benzylpenicillin, commonly referred to as penicillin G, is effective against both Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria. It is unstable in acid." [PMID:4610013]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "Penicillin G" EXACT []
synonym: "benzopenicillin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5904

[Term]
id: ARO:3000633
name: phenoxymethylpenicillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Phenoxymethylpenicillin, or penicillin V, is a penicillin derivative that is acid stable but less active than benzylpenicillin (penicillin G)." [PMID:3924086]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "penicillin V" EXACT []
synonym: "phenomycilline" EXACT []
synonym: "phenopenicillin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6869

[Term]
id: ARO:3000634
name: propicillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Propicillin is an orally taken penicillin derivative that has high absorption but poor activity." [PMID:14056922, PMID:3588519]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "levopropicillin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:92879

[Term]
id: ARO:3000635
name: dicloxacillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Dicloxacillin is a penicillin derivative that has an extra chlorine atom in comparison to cloxacillin. While more active than cloxacillin, its high affinity for serum protein reduces its activity in human serum in vitro." [PMID:3588519, PMID:3764352]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "dicloxacilin" EXACT []
synonym: "dicloxacycline" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:18381

[Term]
id: ARO:3000636
name: flucloxacillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Flucloxacillin is similar to cloxacillin, with an extra additional fluorine atom." [PMID:3588519]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "floxacillin" EXACT []
synonym: "floxapen" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:21319

[Term]
id: ARO:3000637
name: ampicillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Ampicillin is a penicillin derivative that is highly acid stable, with its activity similar to benzylpenicillin." [PMID:44765, PMID:3224398]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "AMP" EXACT []
synonym: "Principen" EXACT []
synonym: "ampicillin acid" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6249

[Term]
id: ARO:3000638
name: azlocillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Azlocillin is a semisynthetic derivative of penicillin that is notably active against Ps. aeruginosa and other Gram-negative bacteria." [PMID:6369480]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "AZL" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6479523

[Term]
id: ARO:3000639
name: mezlocillin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Mezlocillin is a penicillin derivative taken parenterally." [PMID:6369480]
is_a: ARO:3000008 ! penam
synonym: "mezlin" EXACT []
synonym: "mezlocillin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:656511

[Term]
id: ARO:3000640
name: doripenem
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Doripenem is a carbapenem with a broad range of activity against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, and along with meropenem, it is the most active beta-lactam antibiotic against Pseudomonas aeruginosa. It inhibits bacterial cell wall synthesis." [PMID:15047550, PMID:16307551]
is_a: ARO:0000020 ! carbapenem
synonym: "doribax" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:73303

[Term]
id: ARO:3000641
name: cefalexin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefalexin is a cephalosporin antibiotic that causes filamentation. It is resistant to staphylococcal beta-lactamase, but degraded by enterobacterial beta-lactamases." [PMID:4559812]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "LEX" EXACT []
synonym: "cephalexin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:27447

[Term]
id: ARO:3000642
name: cefadroxil
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefadroxil, or p-hydroxycephalexin, is an cephalosporin antibiotic similar to cefalexin." [PMID:3542485]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CFR" EXACT []
synonym: "p-hydroxycephalexin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:47965

[Term]
id: ARO:3000643
name: cefotiam
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefotiam is a cephalosporin antibiotic with similar activity to cefuroxime but more active against enterobacteria. It is consumed orally as the prodrug cefotiam hexetil." [PMID:18611654]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "cefotiamum" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:43708

[Term]
id: ARO:3000644
name: cefaclor
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefaclor is a semisynthetic cephalosporin derived from cephalexin. It has broad-spectrum antibiotic activity." [PMID:10435677]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
