[Term]
id: ARO:3000645
name: cefotaxime
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefotaxime is a semisynthetic cephalosporin taken parenterally. It is resistant to most beta-lactamases and active against Gram-negative rods and cocci due to its aminothiazoyl and methoximino functional groups." [PMID:2083516]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CTX" EXACT []
synonym: "cefotaxime acid" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5742673

[Term]
id: ARO:3000646
name: cefixime
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefixime is a cephalosporin resistant to most beta-lactamases. It is active against many enterobacteria, but activity against staphylococci is poor." [PMID:2684593]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CFM" EXACT []
synonym: "necopen" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5362065

[Term]
id: ARO:3000647
name: cefpodoxime
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefpodoxime is a semisynthetic cephalosporin that acts similarly to cefotaxime with broad-spectrum activity. It is stable to many plasmid-mediated beta-lactamses. Cefpodoxime is consumed as the prodrug cefpodoxime proxetil." [PMID:18611588, PMID:1280571]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CPD" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6335986

[Term]
id: ARO:3000648
name: ceftibuten
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Ceftibuten is a semisynthetic cephalosporin active against Gram-negative bacilli. It is resistant against many plasmid-mediated beta-lactamases." [PMID:9296244, PMID:7520858]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CTB" EXACT []
synonym: "Cedax" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5282242

[Term]
id: ARO:3000649
name: cefditoren
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefditoren is a semisynthetic cephalosporin active against staphylococci, streptococci, and and most enterobacteria. It is resistant to staphylococcal and most enterobacterial beta-lactamases, and is usually taken as the prodrug cefditoren pivoxil." [PMID:7813385]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CDN" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:9571074

[Term]
id: ARO:3000650
name: cefdinir
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefdinir is similar to cefixime with a modified side-chain at its 7-amino position. It also shares similar activity with cefixime but is more active against staphylococci. It has also be shown to enhance phagocytosis." [PMID:8026155]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CDR" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6915944

[Term]
id: ARO:3000651
name: ceftaroline
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Ceftaroline is a novel cephalosporin active against methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus. Like other cephalosporins it binds penicillin-binding proteins to inhibit cell wall synthesis. It strongly binds with PBP2a, associated with methicillin resistance. It is taken orally as the prodrug ceftaroline fosamil." [PMID:18827379, PMID:27721280, PMID:21467022]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "CPT" EXACT []
synonym: "T91825" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:9852982

[Term]
id: ARO:3000659
name: gatifloxacin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Gatifloxacin is an 8-methoxy, 7-piperazinyl, 6-fluoroquinolone that can be taken orally or by intravenous administration. It is active against most Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, but inactive against non-fermenting Gram-negative rods including Pseudomonas aeruginosa." [PMID:8522459]
is_a: ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
synonym: "AM-1155" EXACT []
synonym: "Tequin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5379

[Term]
id: ARO:3000661
name: nalidixic acid
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Nalidixic acid is a quinolone derivative of naphthyridine active against many enterobacteria, but ineffective against Ps aeruginosa, Gram-positive bacteria, and anaerobes. Acquired resistance is common in nalidixic acid treatments." [PMID:18159374]
is_a: ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
synonym: "nalidixin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:4421

[Term]
id: ARO:3000662
name: norfloxacin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Norfloxacin is a 6-fluoro, 7-piperazinyl quinolone with a wide range of activity against Gram-negative bacteria. It is inactive against most anaerobes." [PMID:3908074]
is_a: ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
xref: PubChem:4539

[Term]
id: ARO:3000666
name: sparfloxacin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Sparfloxacin is a dimethylpiperazinyl difluoroquinolone that acts by inhibiting DNA gyrase. It is active against aerobic Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, as well as some mycobacteria. It has moderate activity against some anaerobes." [PMID:1317145]
is_a: ARO:0000001 ! fluoroquinolone antibiotic
synonym: "Zagam" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:60464

[Term]
id: ARO:3000676
