[Term]
id: ARO:3000749
name: beta-lactam sensitive penicillin-binding protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Penicillin-binding proteins (PBPs) are responsible for transpeptidation, joining subunits to form peptidoglycan. They are numbered according to descending molecular weight, and may vary between species. These numbers represent the PBPs of E. coli. Inhibition of the larger PBPs responsible for transpeptidation (1-3) are lethal. Smaller PBPs (4-6) are involed in carboxypeptidation; inhibition of these is non-lethal." [PMID:3055170]
