[Term]
id: ARO:3000823
name: ramA
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "RamA (resistance antibiotic multiple) is a positive regulator of AcrAB-TolC and leads to high level multidrug resistance in Klebsiella pneumoniae, Salmonella enterica, and Enterobacter aerugenes, increasing the expression of both the mar operon as well as AcrAB. RamA also decreases OmpF expression." [PMID:15215103, PMID:7551053, PMID:18577510, PMID:12936981]
