name: ceftizoxime
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Ceftizoxime is a third-generation cephalosporin and broad spectrum beta-lactam antibiotic. Ceftizoxime causes bacterial cell lysis through peptidoglycan cross-linking inhibition by binding to PBPs." [PMID:6326062]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "ZOX" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:6533629

[Term]
id: ARO:3004008
name: cephapirin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cephapirin is a first-generation cephalosporin and broad spectrum beta-lactam antibiotic. Inactivation of penicillin-binding proteins through cephapirin binding disrupts peptidoglycan cross-linking, resulting in cell lysis." []
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "HAP" EXACT []
synonym: "cefadyl" EXACT []
synonym: "cefapirin" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:30699

[Term]
id: ARO:3004009
name: cefradine
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Cefradine is a first-generation cephalosporin and broad spectrum beta-lactam antibiotic. Cefradine binding to penicillin-binding proteins disrupts cell wall peptidoglycan cross-linkage, resulting in cell lysis." [PMID:4572639]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "Cephradine" EXACT []
synonym: "RAD" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:38103

[Term]
id: ARO:3004016
name: loracarbef
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Loracarbef is a second-generation cephalosporin (carbacephem) and broad spectrum beta-lactam antibiotic. Loracarbef inhibits PBPs through binding, disrupting peptidoglycan cell wall cross-linkage and resulting in cell death." [PMID:8453172, PMID:3501757]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "Lorabid" EXACT []
synonym: "Loracarbefum" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:5284585

[Term]
id: ARO:3004017
name: moxalactam
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Moxalactam (Latamoxef) is a broad spectrum cephalosporin (oxacephem) and beta-lactam antibiotic. Moxalactam binding to PBPs inhibits peptidoglycan cross-linkage in the cell wall, resulting in cell death. Moxalactam is proposed to be effective against meningitides as it passes the blood-brain barrier." [PMID:315938, PMID:6218558]
is_a: ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
synonym: "Latamoxef" EXACT []
xref: PubChem:47499

[Term]
id: ARO:3004083
name: AcrEF-TolC confers resistance to ciprofloxacin
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "AcrEF-TolC efflux pump system of E. coli confers resistance to fluoroquinolones (ciprofloxacin)." [PMID:10952561, PMID:16267305]
is_a: ARO:3000503 ! AcrEF-TolC
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000036 ! ciprofloxacin

[Term]
id: ARO:3004243
name: RbpA bacterial RNA polymerase-binding protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "RbpA is a family of bacterial RNA polymerase-binding proteins, which acts as a transcription factor and binds to the sigma subunit of RNA polymerase." [PMID:22570422, PMID:16629670]
is_a: ARO:3000507 ! rifampin-resistant RNA polymerase-binding protein
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000157 ! rifamycin antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3004253
name: vanUG
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "vanUG is a vanG variant found in the vanG gene cluster." [PMID:11036060, PMID:16723588, PMID:14617152]
is_a: ARO:3000575 ! vanU
relationship: part_of ARO:3000257 ! glycopeptide resistance gene cluster VanG

[Term]
id: ARO:3004254
name: vanVB
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "vanVB is a vanV variant found in the vanB gene cluster. It is found in some but not all vanB operons in E. faecalis, suggesting the existence of varied gene compositions in vanB operons." [PMID:21482081]
is_a: ARO:3002916 ! vanV
relationship: part_of ARO:3000238 ! glycopeptide resistance gene cluster VanB

[Term]
id: ARO:3004256
name: Bleomycin resistant protein
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Bleomycin resistant proteins (BRP) confer resistance to bleomycin and to bleomycin-like molecules." [PMID:22290943, PMID:18791008]
is_a: ARO:3001207 ! gene involved in antibiotic sequestration
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000081 ! glycopeptide antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3004277
name: General Bacterial Porin (GBP)
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "General bacterial porins are a family of porins found in the outer membrane of Gram-negative bacteria. They catalyze the energy-independent transport of small molecules across the outer membranes of bacteria. Most of the porins of these family are homotrimeric and have variable selectivity, ranging from being cation-selective, anion-selective or selective for different compounds. The most well characterized members of this family are the OmpF and OmpC porins of Escherichia coli. This family is also known as the classical porins." [PMID:18997824]
is_a: ARO:3000270 ! protein modulating permeability to antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3004281
name: General Bacterial Porin with reduced permeability to beta-lactams
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "These are GBPs that are associated with decreased susceptibility to beta-lactams either through mutations in the porin protein, absence of the porin protein, or expression of the porin protein." []
is_a: ARO:3004277 ! General Bacterial Porin (GBP)
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000004 ! monobactam
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000020 ! carbapenem
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000032 ! cephalosporin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000044 ! cephamycin
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3000008 ! penam
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:3003706 ! penem

[Term]
id: ARO:3004556
name: dfrB7
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "A dihydrofolate reductase and trimethoprim resistance gene identified on an integron in multidrug-resistant gram-negative bacteria" [PMID:21627486]
is_a: ARO:3001218 ! trimethoprim resistant dihydrofolate reductase dfr
synonym: "dfrB8" EXACT []

[Term]
id: ARO:3004650
name: tetU
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "Tetracycline-resistant determinant encoded on the plasmid pKQ10 in Enterococcus faecium" [PMID:8700968]
is_a: ARO:0010002 ! major facilitator superfamily (MFS) antibiotic efflux pump
relationship: confers_resistance_to_antibiotic ARO:0000051 ! tetracycline

[Term]
id: ARO:3005036
name: BLMT
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "BLMT is a bleomycin (Bm) resistance protein, encoded by the ble gene on the transposon Tn5. This protein confers a survival advantage to Escherichia coli host cells. BLMT confers resistance to bleomycin." []
is_a: ARO:3004256 ! Bleomycin resistant protein

[Term]
id: ARO:3005040
name: YajC
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "YajC interacts with the AcrAB-TolC efflux pump in a way that in uncharacterized but is shown to grant increased fitness in the presence of linezolid, rifampicin, and vancomycin." [PMID:31871033]
is_a: ARO:3000748 ! subunit of efflux pump conferring antibiotic resistance
relationship: participates_in ARO:3000384 ! AcrAB-TolC

[Term]
id: ARO:3005049
name: CrcB
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "CrcB is part of the Camphor Resistance Protein Family. It confers resistance to aminoglycoside antibiotics." [PMID:23405357]
is_a: ARO:3000112 ! multidrug and toxic compound extrusion (MATE) transporter
relationship: confers_resistance_to_drug_class ARO:0000016 ! aminoglycoside antibiotic

[Term]
id: ARO:3005350
name: DfrB9
namespace: antibiotic_resistance
def: "DfrB9 is a dihydrofolate reductase that confers resistant to Trimethoprim. Detected directly from NCBI and submitted without publication." []
is_a: ARO:3001218 ! trimethoprim resistant dihydrofolate reductase dfr
synonym: "trimethoprim-resistant dihydrofolate reductase DfrB9" EXACT []
